    Plain text  Screening data from Clusterflick - clusterflick.com (CC BY 4.0)

The licence also asks that you indicate whether you changed the data.


What is not licensed
--------------------

Matched showings carry a `themoviedb` object — and, for events covering more
than one film, a `themoviedbs` array — holding `id`, `title`, `releaseDate` and
`summary` from The Movie Database. The `summary` is TMDB's own synopsis text.

That content belongs to TMDB and is used under the TMDB API terms of use.
Clusterflick cannot sublicense it, so it is excluded from the CC BY 4.0 grant
above. Your use of those fields is governed by TMDB's terms:

    https://www.themoviedb.org/api-terms-of-use

If you show any of it, read TMDB's attribution requirements and follow whatever
they ask for at the time — it is theirs to set, not ours to restate:

    https://www.themoviedb.org/api-terms-of-use#:~:text=3.%20Attribution

If you only want the CC BY 4.0 material, drop the `themoviedb` and
`themoviedbs` keys — the id in them is still useful as a join key if you hold
your own TMDB licence.


